# AIG Architecture Rules

Read `AGENTS.md` for full context. This rule enforces the hard module
boundaries every change must respect.

## Forbidden imports

- `lib/aig/**` MUST NOT import from `lib/db/**`, `lib/arcade/**`, `lib/ai/**`,
  or any package that performs I/O (`postgres`, `@arcadeai/arcadejs`, `ai`,
  `@ai-sdk/*`, `node:fs`, `node:net`, `fetch`).
- `app/**` and `components/**` MUST NOT import `lib/db/**` or `lib/arcade/**`
  directly. Use a route handler or server action.
- Nothing outside `lib/env.ts` reads `process.env`.
- Nothing outside `lib/logger.ts` constructs a `pino` logger.

## Side-effect placement

- DB calls: `lib/db/queries.ts` (Drizzle queries only).
- Arcade calls: `lib/arcade/client.ts` and `lib/arcade/tools.ts`.
- LLM calls: `lib/ai/plan-agent.ts` and `lib/aig/repair.ts` (via `lib/ai/anthropic.ts`).
- HTTP boundaries: `app/api/**/route.ts` only.

## TypeScript hygiene

- No `any`. Use `unknown` + zod parse, or a precise generic.
- `import type` for type-only imports (`verbatimModuleSyntax` enforces).
- Zod schemas live next to the route handler / function that uses them, or
  in `lib/aig/types.ts` if they are domain primitives.
- Result types: prefer `{ ok: true, data } | { ok: false, error }` for any
  function that can fail in a non-exceptional way. Throw only for invariants.

## State machine

- Any change to intent status MUST go through `assertTransition()`.
- New transitions require a unit test in `tests/unit/state.test.ts`.

## Repair changes

- See `.cursor/rules/20-repair.mdc`.
